<section image-layout="blank" id="t4ZxBoTxf-"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="MfhNM8-B5r"><h2>Different actions do different jobs</h2><p font-size="18pt"><b>Call out O, S or C for each tile:</b> ozone recovery, sun safety or climate action. Be ready to explain why.</p><grid spacing="small"><grid-item id="OeEMAGGiTp" cell-style="outline" padding="12pt 16pt" colspan="20"><p font-size="18pt"><b>A</b> Countries phase out ozone-depleting chemicals.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="11df_VJl8z" cell-style="outline" padding="12pt 16pt" colspan="20"><p font-size="18pt"><b>B</b> A trained technician services an old cooling unit.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="P9l2pcvFle" cell-style="outline" padding="12pt 16pt" colspan="20"><p font-size="18pt"><b>C</b> Wear a hat and seek shade.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ajZkHc6U-9" cell-style="outline" padding="12pt 16pt" colspan="20"><p font-size="18pt"><b>D</b> Use sunscreen as directed.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="oLJchbuwPj" cell-style="outline" padding="12pt 16pt" colspan="20"><p font-size="18pt"><b>E</b> Ask adults to choose lower-warming cooling options.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="4wIKpzA2K_" cell-style="outline" padding="12pt 16pt" colspan="20"><p font-size="18pt"><b>F</b> Save energy at home or school.</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="dp_Fur9vW9" background-color="palette-3" padding="12pt 16pt" colspan="20"><h3>O · Ozone recovery</h3><p font-size="18pt">Cuts ozone-depleting substances.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="t4IWU50coE" background-color="palette-2" padding="12pt 16pt" colspan="20"><h3>S · Sun safety</h3><p font-size="18pt">Protects skin from UV now.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="HrmAVrEEUP" background-color="accent" padding="12pt 16pt" colspan="20"><h3>C · Climate action</h3><p font-size="18pt">Reduces warming—a different job.</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item vertical-align="center" colspan="48"><p font-size="18pt"><b>Remember:</b> HFCs do not deplete ozone, but many can warm the climate.</p></grid-item><grid-item vertical-align="center" text-color="#486875" colspan="12"><p role="caption" align="right">Source: <a href="https://www.unep.org/news-and-stories/press-release/ozone-layer-recovery-track-helping-avoid-global-warming-05degc">UNEP</a></p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Sorting key: A and B = ozone recovery. C and D = sun safety. E and F = climate action. Emphasize that children should not handle refrigerants or service cooling equipment; that work belongs to trained adults.</p></notes></section>